# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate a 127-qubit kicked-Ising model for the latest version of Pauli propagation"
msgstr "I-simulate ang 127-qubit na kicked-Ising model para sa pinakabagong bersyon ng Pauli propagation"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate a 127-qubit kicked-Ising model"
msgstr "I-simulate ang 127-qubit na kicked-Ising model"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"addons/pauli-prop/guides/simulate-127-q-kicked-ising.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this guide we use the ``pauli-prop`` package to classically simulate the time dynamics of a 127-qubit kicked-Ising model on a heavy-hex lattice and approximate the single-site magnetization, $\\langle Z_{62} \\rangle$. The Hamiltonian considered is:\n"
msgstr "Sa gabay na ito, gagamitin natin ang ``pauli-prop`` package para i-simulate nang classical ang time dynamics ng isang 127-qubit na kicked-Ising model sa heavy-hex lattice at tantiyahin ang single-site magnetization, $\\langle Z_{62} \\rangle$. Ang Hamiltonian na isinasaalang-alang ay:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$H = -J\\sum\\limits_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_iZ_j + h\\sum\\limits_iX_i$\n"
msgstr "$H = -J\\sum\\limits_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_iZ_j + h\\sum\\limits_iX_i$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $J>0$ describes the coupling of nearest-neighbor spins, $i<j$, and $h$ is the global transverse field. A first-order Trotter decomposition of the time-evolved operator will be implemented as a quantum circuit, $U$, over $20$ Trotter steps. The coupling constant, $J$, will be fixed at $J=-\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ such that $U$ is Clifford any time $h\\mod\\frac{\\pi}{2}=0$.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $J>0$ ay naglalarawan ng coupling ng mga magkatabing spin, $i<j$, at ang $h$ ay ang global na transverse field. Ang first-order na Trotter decomposition ng time-evolved na operator ay ipapatupad bilang isang quantum circuit, $U$, sa loob ng $20$ Trotter step. Ang coupling constant, $J$, ay ifi-fix sa $J=-\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ kaya't Clifford ang $U$ tuwing $h\\mod\\frac{\\pi}{2}=0$.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Workflow:\n"
msgstr "Daloy ng trabaho:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create quantum circuits implementing the Trotterized Ising model\n"
msgstr "Gumawa ng mga quantum circuit na nagpapatupad ng Trotterized na Ising model\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Vary $h$ between Clifford points, $0.0$ and $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\n"
msgstr "Baryahin ang $h$ sa pagitan ng mga Clifford point, $0.0$ at $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a site in the middle of the lattice (qubit $62$) and estimate the magnetization after $20$ Trotter steps for each circuit\n"
msgstr "Pumili ng site sa gitna ng lattice (qubit $62$) at tantiyahin ang magnetization pagkatapos ng $20$ Trotter step para sa bawat circuit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Observe the magnetization roll off from $1.0$ to $0.0$ as $h$ moves from one Clifford point to another\n"
msgstr "Obserbahan ang pagbaba ng magnetization mula $1.0$ hanggang $0.0$ habang lumilipat ang $h$ mula sa isang Clifford point patungo sa isa pa\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create circuits {#create-circuits}"
msgstr "Gumawa ng mga circuit {#create-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, we use ``FakeSherbrooke`` from ``qiskit-ibm-runtime`` to get the edge indices for the coupling map of the 127-qubit Eagle QPU. Once we have the edge indices, we create the Trotter circuits for the varying values of $h$ we want to simulate. The circuits will implement a first-order Trotterization of the Hamiltonian using 20 Trotter steps and 5420 gates.\n"
msgstr "Una, gagamitin natin ang ``FakeSherbrooke`` mula sa ``qiskit-ibm-runtime`` para makuha ang mga edge index para sa coupling map ng 127-qubit na Eagle QPU. Kapag mayroon na tayong mga edge index, gagawa tayo ng mga Trotter circuit para sa iba't ibang halaga ng $h$ na gusto nating i-simulate. Ipapatupad ng mga circuit ang first-order na Trotterization ng Hamiltonian gamit ang 20 Trotter step at 5420 gate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate the time dynamics with Pauli propagation {#simulate-the-time-dynamics-with-pauli-propagation}"
msgstr "I-simulate ang time dynamics gamit ang Pauli propagation {#simulate-the-time-dynamics-with-pauli-propagation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, we specify the observable, $O$, we want to measure. In this case, we estimate $\\langle Z_{62} \\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, tutukuyin natin ang observable, $O$, na gusto nating sukatin. Sa kasong ito, tinatantiya natin ang $\\langle Z_{62} \\rangle$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To study the magnetization between Clifford points, we approximately propagate $O$ to the beginning of the circuit, $U$, resulting in a new observable, $O^\\prime \\approx U^{\\dagger}OU$.\n"
msgstr "Para pag-aralan ang magnetization sa pagitan ng mga Clifford point, tinatantiya nating i-propagate ang $O$ pabalik sa simula ng circuit, $U$, na magreresulta sa bagong observable, $O^\\prime \\approx U^{\\dagger}OU$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"During propagation, the number of terms in the evolved observable grows exponentially in the number of gates, so it is usually necessary to limit how large it can grow. Here, we limit the number of terms in $O^\\prime$ to $10^5$ and truncate terms with coefficients smaller than $10^{-5}$. Truncating terms results in some error.\n"
"Once we have $O^\\prime$, we can easily estimate the expectation value, $\\langle0|U^{\\dagger}OU|0\\rangle = \\langle0|O^\\prime|0\\rangle$, by summing the coefficients of the diagonal terms in $O^\\prime$ (terms consisting only of ``I`` or ``Z`` on all qubits).\n"
msgstr ""
"Habang nagpo-propagate, exponential na lumalaki ang bilang ng mga term sa evolved na observable ayon sa bilang ng mga gate, kaya karaniwang kailangang limitahan kung gaano ito kalaki. Dito, nililimitahan natin ang bilang ng mga term sa $O^\\prime$ sa $10^5$ at tinatanggal ang mga term na may coefficient na mas maliit sa $10^{-5}$. Nagdudulot ng kaunting error ang pag-truncate ng mga term.\n"
"Kapag mayroon na tayong $O^\\prime$, madali nating matatantiya ang expectation value, $\\langle0|U^{\\dagger}OU|0\\rangle = \\langle0|O^\\prime|0\\rangle$, sa pamamagitan ng pagsasama-sama ng mga coefficient ng mga diagonal na term sa $O^\\prime$ (mga term na binubuo lamang ng ``I`` o ``Z`` sa lahat ng qubit).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We set ``frame='h'`` to specify we want to evolve the observable in the Heisenberg framework ($U^{\\dagger}OU$). Use ``frame=s`` for Schrödinger evolution ($UOU^{\\dagger}$).\n"
msgstr "Itinakda natin ang ``frame='h'`` para tukuyin na gusto nating i-evolve ang observable sa Heisenberg framework ($U^{\\dagger}OU$). Gamitin ang ``frame=s`` para sa Schrödinger evolution ($UOU^{\\dagger}$).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize {#visualize}"
msgstr "I-visualize {#visualize}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we plot the magnetization as a function of $h$. When $h=0$, the circuit does not affect the initial state in the computational basis, and we know $\\langle0|O|0\\rangle = 1.0$. As $h$ moves further from $0$, the magnetization decays monotonically until $h$ reaches the next Clifford angle, $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, and the magnetization converges to $0$.\n"
msgstr "Panghuli, ipi-plot natin ang magnetization bilang function ng $h$. Kapag $h=0$, hindi naaapektuhan ng circuit ang initial state sa computational basis, at alam nating $\\langle0|O|0\\rangle = 1.0$. Habang lumalayo ang $h$ mula sa $0$, monotonic na bumababa ang magnetization hanggang umabot ang $h$ sa susunod na Clifford angle, $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, at nagko-converge ang magnetization sa $0$.\n"

